                <pb facs="0738" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg724"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Roberts, Spanish
                        minister, to Mr. Fish, Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Spain at
                            Washington</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1869-04-15"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 15,
                    1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p>The minister plenipotentiary of Spain has had the honor to receive the note of
                    14th instant, in which the honorable Secretary of State pleased to send him copy
                    of a communication from the minister of Peru, dated the 9th, explaining the
                    causes which gave occasion for the touching at Puerto Naranjo, in the island of
                    Cuba, of the Peruvian monitor Manco Capac.</p>
                <p>The undersigned has already sent to his government these satisfactory
                    communications, and presents his thanks to the honorable Secretary Fish for his
                    attention, availing himself of this occasion to offer to him the expression of
                    his highest consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MAURICIO LOPEZ ROBERTS.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Honorable <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi><lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Of the United States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
